add('p1','这一步要回答：8-3--6-5 中，5 的父节点是谁？二叉树的每个节点最多有两个有次序的孩子，称为左、右孩子。根是没有父节点的节点；深度是从根走到节点的边数，所以根深度为 0。先序遍历按“节点本身、完整左子树、完整右子树”访问；子树包括该节点和它的所有后代。','Who is the parent of 5 in 8-3--6-5? A binary tree gives each node at most two ordered children, left and right. The root has no parent. Depth counts edges from the root, so the root has depth 0. Preorder visits a node, its entire left subtree, then its entire right subtree. A subtree contains a node and all its descendants.')
add('handHint','把一组连续短横线和紧随的完整整数称为一个词元。先读每个词元的深度，再按“接入一个节点”观察新增边；返回可撤回。L / R 表示左 / 右边，缩进表示深度，不表示数值大小。# 是从 0 开始的词元编号。窄屏可聚焦树并水平滚动。','A token is a run of dashes followed by one complete integer. Read each token’s depth, then use “Attach one node” to inspect the new edge; Back undoes it. L / R mark left / right edges. Indentation means depth, not numerical order. # is a zero-based token ID. On narrow screens, focus the tree to scroll horizontally.')
add('tokens','手算词元：(0,8), (1,3), (2,6), (1,5)。括号内依次为深度、值。','Hand tokens: (0,8), (1,3), (2,6), (1,5). Each pair is (depth, value).')
for i,zh,en in [(0,'还未接入节点。先找没有短横线的 8。','No nodes attached. Start with 8, which has no dashes.'),(1,'8 深度 0，成为根。','8 has depth 0 and becomes the root.'),(2,'3 深度 1，只能接到深度 0 的 8。先序先走左边，所以是 8 的左孩子。','3 has depth 1, so its parent is depth-0 node 8. Preorder visits left first, so attach it on the left.'),(3,'6 深度 2，比 3 深一层，所以接为 3 的左孩子。','6 has depth 2, one level below 3, so it becomes the left child of 3.'),(4,'5 深度 1，需要深度 0 的父节点 8。6 和 3 的子树都已结束；8 左边已有 3，因此 5 接到右边。','5 has depth 1 and needs depth-0 parent 8. The subtrees of 6 and 3 have ended. Since 8 already has left child 3, attach 5 on the right.')]:add('hand'+str(i),zh,en)
add('handPrev','撤回一个节点','Undo one node');add('handNext','接入一个节点','Attach one node')
add('limits','官方保证：只有一个孩子时，这个孩子一定在左边。输入来自一棵有效的原树；1–1000 个节点，节点值 1–10⁹，可以重复。没有空树输入。返回根节点对象，示例中的数组只是树的层序表示，不是返回类型。','Official guarantees: an only child is always the left child. The input encodes a valid original tree with 1–1000 nodes, values 1–10⁹, and possible repeated values. There is no empty-tree input. Return the root object; example arrays describe trees in level order and are not the return type.')
add('p2','这一步要回答：能否不维护路径，也找到左右子树？把词元切成子树即可。对根 8，后面的 3 深度为 1，开始左子树；6 深度为 2，仍属于 3；下一个深度回到 1 的 5，开始右子树。于是切成 [3,6] 和 [5]。再切 [3,6] 得到根 3 和左子树 [6]；处理完返回后，8 再处理 [5]。','Can we find the two subtrees without maintaining a path? Split the tokens. After root 8, depth-1 token 3 begins the left subtree. Depth-2 token 6 stays inside it. The next depth-1 token, 5, begins the right subtree. Split into [3,6] and [5]. Splitting [3,6] gives root 3 with left subtree [6]; after that returns, 8 processes [5].')
add('baseline','下面是可独立核对的基线。ts 是已解析的 (深度,值) 列表；返回 (值,左树,右树) 三元组，None 表示没有孩子，便于比较结构，并非官方返回对象。空列表终止递归；每次调用都扫描剩余词元寻找右子树起点，并复制子列表。在 n 个节点的单链上，反复扫描 n−1、n−2、… 个词元，扫描与复制均为 O(n²)；先解析还要 O(L)，L 为全部字符数。保留的递归子列表最坏占 O(n²) 空间。','This independently checkable baseline takes parsed (depth,value) tokens ts. It returns nested (value,left,right) triples, with None for no child, to compare structure; this is not the official return object. Empty lists end recursion. Each call scans the remaining tokens for the right-subtree boundary and copies sublists. A chain of n nodes repeatedly scans n−1, n−2, … tokens, giving O(n²) scanning and copying plus O(L) initial parsing, where L counts all characters. Retained recursive sublists can also occupy O(n²) space.')
add('baseSource','查看切分基线 Python','Inspect the splitting baseline in Python')
add('wrongRule','为什么不能“接到前一个节点”？在 8-3--6-5 中，5 的前一个节点是 6，但 6 深度 2，不能作深度 1 的 5 的父节点。为什么不能只凭深度随便选左右？若删去“独子在左”保证，8-3 既可能是左孩子，也可能是右孩子，信息不足。','Why not attach to the previous node? In 8-3--6-5, the previous node is 6 at depth 2, which cannot parent depth-1 node 5. Why not choose either side from depth alone? Without the only-child-is-left guarantee, 8-3 could mean a left child or a right child: the encoding would be ambiguous.')
add('bridge','重复扫描其实都在问“哪些子树已经结束”。走到 5 时，我们只需把路径 [8,3,6] 尾部的 6、3 移除，剩下 8 就是父节点。已经接好的边仍保留；移除的是候选祖先，不是删除树节点。','The repeated scans ask which subtrees have ended. At 5, remove 6 and then 3 from the end of path [8,3,6]; the remaining 8 is its parent. Existing edges remain: we remove candidate ancestors, not tree nodes.')
add('p3','这一步要回答：下一个节点的父节点藏在哪里？栈是只从末尾取出元素的列表。每次接入后，path 栈保存根到最近接入节点的祖先路径，槽位 0、1、2 就是深度。读到深度 depth 后，弹出末尾元素，直到 len(path) = depth；此时栈顶在 depth−1 层，是新节点的父节点。先接空的左边，否则接右边，再把新节点压入路径。','Where is the next node’s parent? A stack is a list whose elements are removed from its end. After each attachment, path stores the ancestor path from the root to the most recently attached node; slots 0, 1, 2 are depths. After reading depth, pop from the end until len(path) = depth. The top is now at depth−1 and is the new node’s parent. Fill its empty left side, otherwise its right side, then push the new node.')
add('formula','接入前：len(path) = depth；接入后：len(path) = depth + 1，path[depth] = 新节点。','Before attachment: len(path) = depth; after attachment: len(path) = depth + 1, path[depth] = new node.')
